From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:14:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] stamp element indices on the svg snapshot

Elements inside an inline <svg> never get a layout box: the svg is one
atomic box and its subtree is serialized to a usvg tree at construct
time. To measure one of them (getBoundingClientRect on a <rect>), the
engine has to find the DOM node again in that tree, and the only thing
usvg carries through the parse is the element id.

Add a snapshot-only serializer entry (write_svg_snapshot_html) that
stamps `id="ks-svg-<n>"` on every descendant without a usable id, where
n is the element's pre-order index under the snapshot root. An index
rather than the node id, because parse_svg_image caches trees on the
exact serialized source and icon systems emit one identical <svg> per
use site (136 inline svgs, 47 distinct, on one heavy page); node ids
would have made every copy a separate parse. svg_snapshot_index recovers
the index for a node the same way, so the two walks must stay in step.

An empty id="" is dropped rather than kept next to the stamp, since a
duplicate attribute fails the whole XML parse. The snapshot root keeps
its open tag untouched because rebuild_svg_snapshot pattern-matches on
it. Plain outer_html is unchanged, so nothing page-visible sees the
synthetic ids.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: serialization moved to node/serialize.rs
and the snapshot source is upstream's svg_source(), so the stamping
lives there instead of a separate write_svg_snapshot_html entry; the
public svg_snapshot_id / Node::svg_snapshot_index API is unchanged.
